{"notice_id": "16552951", "title": "Disability Commission Advisory Board Remote Meeting | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": true, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16552951", "posted_at": "2026-01-13T11:40:00-05:00", "event_datetime": "2026-12-09T22:30:00Z", "address_1": "Remote Meeting", "address_2": "", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  Agenda\n\n\n\n\nMeeting Called to Order\nIntroductions\nApproval of Minutes\nPresentation\nChair’s Report\nCommissioner's Report: Kristen McCosh\nBoard Member Share Outs\nOld Business\nNew Business\nPublic Input\nAdjournment\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Meeting Accommodation Notice \n\n\n\nAll meetings held by the City of Boston are required to be accessible for persons with disabilities under Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA).\nAccommodations are available upon request to any person who requires alternately\nformatted materials, auxiliary aids, or another accommodation to ensure effective communication and access to attend meetings held by City departments and programs.\nPlease allow at least 2 weeks to arrange for accommodations.\nRequests for accommodations may be sent to the contact person for the meeting, or may be forwarded to:\nKristen McCosh, Disability Commissioner and ADA Title II Coordinator\nkristen.mccosh@boston.gov, 617-635-3682 (voice), or 617-635-2541 (TTY).\nInterpretation and translation services are available to you at no cost. If you need them, please contact us at disability@boston.gov or 617-635-3682, as soon as possible.\n\n\n\n\n", "files": [{"file_label": "Official Filed Posting", "file_url": "https://www.boston.gov/sites/default/files/file/2026/01/Dec%202026%20Disability%20Commission%20Advisory%20Board%20Agenda%2012-9-2026.pdf", "download_success": true, "file_hash": "f08d01176e8f93f9f25ad9dd66c81123a1d518559fbf9e715528313aaa2103b0"}], "status": "ok", "checked_at": "2026-08-04T18:19:34.820461+00:00"}
{"notice_id": "16492941", "title": "Boston Retirement Board Meeting | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": false, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16492941", "posted_at": "2025-11-19T11:08:00-05:00", "event_datetime": "2026-12-16T14:00:00Z", "address_1": "Boston City Hall ", "address_2": "1 City Hall Square, Board Room, Room 816", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  The standard administrative session agenda is as follows:\n\n\n\n\nConvene Meeting (Introduction of Members & Guests)\nAdministrative Session Minutes of previous board meeting\nOutstanding/Ongoing Administrative Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Investment Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Financial Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Operations Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Legal Issues\nAdjourn\nThe Board enters Executive Session in order to review applications for disability retirement benefits, accidental death benefits, member survivor allowance benefits, pension forfeiture, as well as litigation strategy.  At the conclusion of the Executive Session, the Board reconvenes in Administrative Session in order to consider the rest of the agenda items, if any, and adjourn.\n\n\n\n\n\n", "files": [{"file_label": "Official Filed Posting", "file_url": "https://www.boston.gov/sites/default/files/file/2025/11/Retirment%20For%202026_1.pdf", "download_success": true, "file_hash": "b75ee84e481db0befebdcfffa2bff88e6e003bc0cd64940ac24b3cc8acf68b08"}], "status": "ok", "checked_at": "2026-08-04T18:19:36.913109+00:00"}
