{"notice_id": "16600791", "title": "Boston Landmarks Commission | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": false, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16600791", "posted_at": "2026-07-17T12:44:00-04:00", "event_datetime": "2026-07-28T20:00:00Z", "address_1": "HTTPS://WWW.ZOOMGOV.COM/J/1653954504 ", "address_2": "", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  Design Review - 4pm\n\n\n\nAPP #26.0829 BLC CHESTNUT HILL RESERVOIR & PUMPING STATIONS: \nProposed Work: Replace a portion of the existing Chestnut      Hill Reservoir Trail and construct new stormwater        management features to improve drainage, including a       new bioretention swale and bioretention rain garden.       CONTINUED FROM 04/28/26\n APP #27.0015 BLC MISSION CHURCH COMPLEX:  \nProposed Work: Expansion of grammar school into        underutilized portions of rectory building with minor       modifications to exterior targeted to interventions to       support the school use in portions of the rectory building.\nAPP #26.0407 BLC TILESTON HOUSE - REAR ADDITION\nProposed Work: Addition to the rear of the existing house      at 13 River Street. \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Administrative Review/Approval\n\n\n\nAPP # 26.1062 BLC ARLINGTON STREET CHURCH, 351 ARLINGTON STREET \nReplace gate at south vestibule entrance.\nAPP # 27.00142BLC BLACKSTONE BLOCK, 16 NORTH STREET \nInstallation of blade sign.\nAPP # 27.0003 BLC BOSTON CITY HALL, 1 CITY HALL SQUARE \nAt interior of building alteration of existing cable suspension system used for temporary art installations located at the 5th floor mezzanine concrete railing.\nAPP # 26.1131 BLC HUTCHINSON BUILDING, 44 PROVINCE STREET\nInstallation of blade sign.\nAPP # 26.1109 BLC DONALD MCKAY HOUSE, 78-80R WHITE STREET\nRepair and replace missing and deteriorated sections of exterior trim and siding.\nAPP # 26.1129 BLC SEARS BUILDING, 401 PARK DRIVE\nExterior rehabilitation of the building including masonry repair and window replacement previously approved in 2024.\nAPP # 27.0034 BLC 400-402 MELNEA CASS BOULVARD, EUSTIS STREET ACDC\nInstallation of two interpretive signs.\nAPP # 26.1150 MHT 1605 TREMONT STREET\nEmergency repair - all work to be done in kind: strip existing roofing and inspect roof, re-shingle area, install 8\" aluminum drip edge, re-flash 2 skylights, remove and replace any rotted wood.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Business Hearing - 6pm\n\n\n\nRATIFICATION OF MEETING MINUTES \nCommission to vote on meeting minutes from July 14, 2026.\nDESIGN REVIEW RECAP AND VOTE\nAPP #26.0829 BLC CHESTNUT HILL RESERVOIR & PUMPING STATIONS:\nProposed Work: Replace a portion of the existing Chestnut      Hill Reservoir Trail and construct new stormwater        management features to improve drainage, including a       new bioretention swale and bioretention rain garden.       CONTINUED FROM 04/28/26\nAPP #27.0015 BLC MISSION CHURCH COMPLEX: \nProposed Work: Expansion of grammar school into        underutilized portions of rectory building with minor       modifications to exterior targeted to interventions to       support the school use in portions of the rectory building.\nAPP #26.0407 BLC TILESTON HOUSE - REAR ADDITION\nProposed Work: Addition to the rear of the existing house      at 13 River Street. \n \nADMINISTRATIVE APPROVAL ITEMS\nReview Motion and Vote\n \nSTUDY REPORTS & DESIGNATIONS\n305.26 - FOLSOM HOUSE, 3-4 FOLSOM AVE., MISSION HILL\n\nVote to upgrade survey rating\nPresentation of Study Report\nPublic feedback on Study Report\nDiscussion of Study Report\nVote to accept Study Report\nVote on Designation\n\nOFFICE OF HISTORIC PRESERVATION UPDATES \nPRESENTATION ON MARKER PROGRAM.  POSTPONED TO THE AUGUST 11, 2026 BUSINESS MEETING. \n \nSTAFF UPDATES\n \nPROJECTED ADJOURNMENT - 7pm\n\n\n\n\n", "files": [{"file_label": "OFFICIAL FILED POSTING", "file_url": "https://www.boston.gov/sites/default/files/file/2026/07/7.28.26%20BLC%20Agenda.pdf", "download_success": true, "file_hash": "3b76e09c806dda346da2608df3239de29d2864fed05