{"notice_id": "16602821", "title": "Zoning Board of Appeal Hearing | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": true, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16602821", "posted_at": "2026-08-03T14:18:00-04:00", "event_datetime": "2026-08-11T13:30:00Z", "address_1": "1 CITY HALL SQUARE", "address_2": "RM 801", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  APPROVAL OF HEARING MINUTES: 9:30AM\n\n\n\nJuly 28, 2026\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  EXTENSIONS: 9:30AM\n\n\n\nCase: BOA-1625031 Address: 26 Lawrence Avenue Ward 14 Applicant: Heather Martin, Chief Operating Office, Heading Hoe, Inc.\nCase: BOA- 1450131 Address: 60-70 Geneva Avenue Ward 14 Applicant: Michael P. Ross, Esq\nCase: BOA- 1526561 Address: 1015 Hyde Park Avenue Ward 18 Applicant: Ryan Spitz, Esq\nCase: BOA- 1553455 Address: 1052 Hyde Park Avenue Ward 18 Applicant: Ryan Spitz, Esq\nCase: BOA- 1019280 Address: 10-12 Bentham Road Ward 15 Applicant: Arlene Cruthrid\nCase: BOA- 1598752 Address: 308 Norwell Street Ward 17 Applicant: Derric Small, Esq\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  BOARD FINAL ARBITER: 9:30AM\n\n\n\nCase: BOA- 1817132 Address: 18 Delle Avenue Ward 10 Applicant: Design Resource Team\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  HEARINGS: 9:30AM\n\n\n\nCase: BOA-1851830 Address: 415-415A Hanover Street Ward 3 Applicant: Phillip Frattaroli Article (s): Art. 54 Section 9 Use: Conditional Outdoor Seating is Conditional. Purpose: Seasonal patio from May 1st to October 31st. This patio is the same that has been in place since 2020\nCase: BOA-1849656 Address: 35 Braddock Park Ward 4 Applicant: Sam Madoff and Lauren Madoff Article(s): Art. 32 Sec. 04 GCOD Applicability Art. 64 Sec. 09 Dimensional Regulations Insufficient rear yard setback Applicable in Residential Sub Purpose: Construction of a new detached accessory GARAGE w/ green space/sitting area above located at the rear of the lot with Private Alley (541) access, serving the existing single-family residence. It's a customary accessory structure consistent with rear lot alley conditions. *Application re a